issues.problem:
Round 7's canonical sentence is right. Four case summaries of the copy rule leave out whether the original is kept or hidden. They are false against measurements, and they contradict the canonical sentence and E-S2.14's own keptcopy sentence (l.2349-2352: 'a Guard part's copy in the Blade or the Grip ... gives those of the part itself so changed'). This is severity (b) and (c).

(1) E-S2.14 l.2330-2331 (new): 'where a copy in a slot its original's outranks changes nothing too (V2's relabel6)'.
(2) Plain words l.678 (new): 'a copy given a less important slot changes nothing (the second reviewer's relabel6)'.
Both are false for a kept original. Case: F2 plus a Ctrl+D copy of its kept Guard part (id 3), relabelled Grip and left in place. Guard outranks Grip (§3.7), and the design stays valid. The verdict keeps the copy, since Grip's name comes first, and cleans part 3. Measured changes:
- balance -0.056986899563318927 -> -0.15698689956331902;
- guardPos 0.6 -> 0.43333;
- reach 3.10187 -> 2.83538;
- bladeLength 2.5 -> 2.4;
- cutIndex 0.425 -> 0.400;
- mass and G unchanged.
This is exactly F2 with part 3 relabelled Grip. My relabel6 was a hidden filler, and my round-6 report scoped it to a hidden part and named this kept case. The summary drops that scope.

(3) Plain words l.651-652: 'a copy given a more important slot than its original's ... counts again among the pieces that cover others, exactly as relabelling the original would'. Case: F2 plus a copy of its kept Grip part (id 2) relabelled Guard. The verdict cleans the copy, and every output of Analyze.run equals F2's. Part 2 itself relabelled Guard leaves no kept Grip part, so that design is invalid.

(4) SPEC §4.4 l.996-997, which V1 also reports: 'a copy of a part in a slot whose name comes after its original's ... is cleaned and changes nothing'. This is false for a hidden part. Case: S4 with filler 17 hidden in the Grip, plus a copy of 17 relabelled Guard (valid). The verdict cleans the copy, but §4.3's priority puts it first (Guard rank 2 before Grip 3), so it takes 17's place:
- mass 1.2911872496778234 -> 1.288800782357806 (-2.3865e-3 kg);
- balance 0.38296413767222037 -> 0.37876627631713933;
- equal to 17 relabelled Guard; f7ac37d gives the same.

Sweep (work\copyrule7.luau, 717 valid cases on the tree): the verdict keeps a kept original's copy exactly when the copy's slot name comes first. That happens in 90 cases (Guard->Blade or Grip, Pommel->Blade, Grip or Guard), and each one equals the original so changed. 18 of them are Guard->Grip copies, and all 18 differ from the build.
